<Docs title="Terminal integrations" intro="Run the explorer, use the Rust crates, or export a Ghostty shader.">
<h2>The command line</h2><pre><code>npx @austindelic/blackhole-cli explore</code></pre><p>The CLI launches the native terminal renderer for your platform. See the repository's <a href="https://github.com/austindelic/blackhole#terminal">terminal guide</a> for available builds and source installation.</p>
<h2 id="rust">Rust and Ratatui</h2><pre><code>cargo install austindelic-blackhole-cli
blackhole</code></pre><p>The terminal renderer uses Rust and Ratatui to present its character grid. Build it from the repository when a prebuilt binary is unavailable, or study the native application as an integration reference.</p><pre><code>git clone https://github.com/austindelic/blackhole.git
cd blackhole
cargo run --release -p austindelic-blackhole-cli</code></pre><p>For embedding in your own Rust application, use <code>austindelic-blackhole</code> and <code>austindelic-blackhole-ratatui</code>. Follow the crates’ public API and example in the <a href="https://github.com/austindelic/blackhole/tree/main/crates">Rust source</a>. The terminal and web runtimes have different rendering constraints; they share a visual direction rather than promising identical output.</p>
<h2 id="ghostty">Ghostty</h2>
<p>The published CLI, version 0.1.0, exports a simple background shader. It does not reproduce the web renderer. The replacement in the repository is not yet released and still needs native visual verification.</p>
<pre><code>npx @austindelic/blackhole-cli@0.1.0 ghostty --out-dir ./blackhole-ghostty</code></pre>
<p>The command copies the shader and its notices, and prints the configuration. It does not change your active settings. For this published version, add:</p>
<pre><code>custom-shader = /absolute/path/blackhole-ghostty/blackhole.glsl
custom-shader-animation = true</code></pre>
<p>Remove that <code>custom-shader</code> line to disable it. Set <code>custom-shader-animation = false</code> to render only when the terminal updates.</p>
<p>See the <a href="https://github.com/austindelic/blackhole/tree/main/integrations/ghostty">replacement's source and verification notes</a> for its three-pass setup and limitations. Those instructions do not apply to the 0.1.0 export.</p>
</Docs>
